OL,3,ASchools in England get extra #500m in
OL,4,Abid to avoid teachers' pay strike
OL,5,
OL,6,FSchools in England are to get around
OL,7,F#500 million in extra funding towards
OL,8,Fthe teachers' pay award this school
OL,9,Fyear, reducing the risk of a strike
OL,10,Fballot by the largest education union.
OL,12,FSchools had been expected to fund some
OL,13,Fof the 3.5% teachers pay increase for
OL,14,Fthe current school year out of their
OL,15,Fexisting budgets, which National
OL,16,FEducation Union (NEU) leaders had
OL,17,Fstrongly objected to.
OL,19,FDaniel Kebede, the General Secretary of
OL,20,Fthe NEU, said the offer of more funding
OL,21,Fwas a "significant" step in
OL,22,Fnegotiations.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
